The registration function is `register<Component>CardsContainerConfig(context)`. It registers a hook under the service key `<COMPONENT>_CARDS_CONTAINER_CONFIG_HOOK`. The hook takes no arguments (it may call React hooks) and returns this object, with every member optional:

```typescript
{
  layout?: 'horizontal' | 'vertical';
  showPagination?: boolean;
  ToolbarElement?: FC<ToolbarElementProps<Row>>;   // filter bar above the cards
  ActionbarElement?: FC<ActionbarElementProps<Row>>;
  CardElement?: FC<CardProps<Row, RowActionDefinitions>>; // one card per row
}
```

A custom `CardElement` must render a `<Grid size={ { sm: 12, md: 6, lg: 4, xl: 4 } }>` as its root so cards line up on all devices.
